# Commit 010 — Enterprise Intelligence & Enterprise Society

## Purpose

Commit 010 establishes the Enterprise Intelligence architecture of Essentials Mart and formally defines the Enterprise Society as a coordinated collection of specialised enterprise intelligence capabilities.

The Enterprise Society exists because Essentials Mart cannot become a globally scalable Household Care Platform while relying on disconnected operational systems and isolated intelligence tools.

Enterprise Intelligence must operate as part of the platform's architecture rather than as a collection of unrelated dashboards.

The architecture must allow intelligence generated in one enterprise domain to become useful evidence for another domain while preserving:

* domain ownership;
* explainability;
* human authority;
* trust;
* privacy;
* auditability;
* economic sustainability;
* scalability.

---

# 1. Why Enterprise Intelligence Exists

Enterprise Intelligence exists to help Essentials Mart understand, operate and continuously improve the enterprise itself.

It provides intelligence across:

* supply;
* inventory;
* warehouses;
* logistics;
* finance;
* people;
* compliance;
* marketing;
* operations;
* retailers;
* suppliers;
* executives;
* workforce;
* customer experience.

Enterprise Intelligence is therefore not a single system.

It is an interconnected set of specialised capabilities operating within clearly defined boundaries.

---

# 2. The Five Enterprise Domain Questions

Every Enterprise Intelligence capability must answer five questions before it is considered architecturally complete.

### 2.1 Why does it exist?

The capability must solve a meaningful enterprise problem.

It must not exist merely because the technology makes it possible.

### 2.2 What does it own?

Every capability must have clearly defined responsibility and authoritative data boundaries.

It must not become a competing source of truth for another domain.

### 2.3 How does it build trust?

Enterprise Intelligence must be:

* explainable;
* auditable;
* governed;
* fair;
* privacy-conscious;
* economically responsible.

### 2.4 How does AI make it better?

AI may improve:

* detection;
* forecasting;
* pattern recognition;
* prioritisation;
* anomaly identification;
* scenario analysis;
* decision support.

AI must assist enterprise decision-makers rather than silently replace them.

### 2.5 Can it operate at 100 million users?

The capability must remain architecturally viable as Essentials Mart expands across:

* millions of households;
* thousands of stores;
* multiple warehouses;
* multiple countries;
* multiple currencies;
* multiple regulatory environments;
* large supplier networks.

---

# 3. Enterprise Intelligence Principle

> **Enterprise Intelligence informs the enterprise; it does not become the enterprise's unchecked decision-maker.**

Intelligence should surface:

* evidence;
* patterns;
* forecasts;
* anomalies;
* risks;
* opportunities;
* relationships.

Human decision-makers retain authority over consequential enterprise decisions.

---

